  "intro": "A 1,000 m² culinary house of culture on the ground floor of the Kant-Garagenpalast, Charlottenburg: Europe's oldest surviving high-rise garage, built in 1930 in the Neue Sachlichkeit style and listed for its double-helix ramp. Four kitchens, a bakery and café, two bars, a gallery and a 300 m² south-facing beer garden under one roof, with a 300-element LED ceiling and eight audio zones, right on the S-Bahn tracks. Opened May 2026.",
  "credit": "Logo and brand identity by Plusminus Studio. Everything else, from concept, vendors and contracts to marketing, sales and day-to-day running, I led as Managing Director.",
